<item><title>Liberia&apos;s House sends US$5.7 billion Bea Mountain deal for review</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-house-sends-us-5-7-billion-bea-mountain-deal-for-f2e4ae/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-house-sends-us-5-7-billion-bea-mountain-deal-for-f2e4ae/</guid><category>Liberia</category><description>The proposed agreement includes 270 megawatts of power projects and road construction, but still needs legislative review and ratification.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 08:58:01 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/lr.jpg" length="31000" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/lr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Liberia’s petroleum regulator sets 2027 deadline for first sector report</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-petroleum-regulator-sets-2027-deadline-for-first-c75643/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-petroleum-regulator-sets-2027-deadline-for-first-c75643/</guid><category>Liberia</category><description>The five-year plan also follows US$13.8 million in budget contributions and eight production-sharing contracts ratified by lawmakers.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:54:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/lr.jpg" length="31000" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/lr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Liberia’s Senate orders inquiry into banknote shortage and high prices</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-senate-orders-inquiry-into-banknote-shortage-and-5c7bec/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-senate-orders-inquiry-into-banknote-shortage-and-5c7bec/</guid><category>Liberia</category><description>The committee is due to examine delays in releasing up to L$79 billion in authorized notes and why currency gains have not lowered commodity prices.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:48:25 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-senate-orders-inquiry-into-banknote-shortage-and-5c7bec/share.jpg" length="44791" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-senate-orders-inquiry-into-banknote-shortage-and-5c7bec/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Liberia’s agriculture minister warns El Niño could cut rice yields by 30 to 50%</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-agriculture-minister-warns-el-nino-could-cut-rice-ca45be/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/lr/liberia-s-agriculture-minister-warns-el-nino-could-cut-rice-ca45be/</guid><category>Liberia</category><description>Dr. J. Alexander Nuetah told lawmakers that erratic rains and heat could disrupt planting and leave rice farmers with little or no harvest.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:38:12 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/lr.jpg" length="31000" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/lr.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
